WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.956 --> 00:00:11.743
Hi I hope you like your new school, but I really miss you here!

2
00:00:13.204 --> 00:00:17.708
This year the drama club is putting on William Shakespeare's Romeo and Juliet.

3
00:00:19.149 --> 00:00:24.072
You probably think I'm playing Romeo since I'm usually the lead in drama club productions.

4
00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:25.793
But you're wrong.

5
00:00:27.895 --> 00:00:29.096
I'm not even in the cast!

6
00:00:30.228 --> 00:00:32.630
Mrs. Geller picked me for stage manager.

7
00:00:34.511 --> 00:00:38.094
I'll be in charge of the sets, sound and lighting, and props.

8
00:00:40.436 --> 00:00:44.019
She said it would be good experience, but it sounds pretty boring to me.

9
00:00:45.860 --> 00:00:47.361
And you know what makes it even worse?

10
00:00:48.942 --> 00:00:51.304
Rose Adams is playing Juliet!

11
00:00:53.666 --> 00:00:56.268
This would have been my chance to get to know her better.

12
00:00:57.748 --> 00:01:01.551
Instead I'm stuck backstage, and Jae gets to be Romeo.

13
00:01:03.213 --> 00:01:05.935
I guess it's good that you moved all the way across the country.

14
00:01:06.755 --> 00:01:08.657
Things around here aren't much fun.

15
00:01:09.718 --> 00:01:10.839
Hope to hear from you soon!

16
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:18.745
Carlos Hey!

17
00:01:19.686 --> 00:01:21.647
Sorry it's been so long since I wrote.

18
00:01:22.388 --> 00:01:23.649
I've been super busy!

19
00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.012
The sets for the play are supposed to be pretty basic.

20
00:01:27.724 --> 00:01:31.266
But we've been working every single afternoon to build what we need.

21
00:01:32.087 --> 00:01:36.810
We just finished the set for the scene where Juliet talks to Romeo from her balcony.

22
00:01:39.111 --> 00:01:40.792
I came up with the idea for the set.

23
00:01:43.173 --> 00:01:48.116
We painted big pieces of cardboard to look like the front of Juliet's house.

24
00:01:49.337 --> 00:01:52.219
Then we cut out a doorway and added a railing.

25
00:01:56.696 --> 00:01:59.758
Rose stands on a platform behind the cardboard front.

26
00:02:01.198 --> 00:02:04.300
It looks just like she's looking over a balcony railing!

27
00:02:06.861 --> 00:02:08.102
We're making props too.

28
00:02:11.143 --> 00:02:15.745
We used wood for daggers and painted the blades with shiny silver paint.

29
00:02:17.626 --> 00:02:21.508
Jae's little brother lent us a giant plastic baseball bat.

30
00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:28.492
We covered it with brown paper to make it look like a wooden club for the fight scene

31
00:02:28.532 --> 00:02:29.173
in act 1.

32
00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:35.318
It's actually fun thinking of ways to make things or adapt them to look realistic for the props.

33
00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:38.501
I have to run now.

34
00:02:39.442 --> 00:02:42.024
We're meeting in a few minutes to discuss sound and lighting.

35
00:02:43.105 --> 00:02:43.906
Talk to you soon!

36
00:02:44.347 --> 00:02:50.112
Carlos I don't know how we're going to get everything done in two weeks!

37
00:02:51.584 --> 00:02:57.048
The cast is rehearsing every afternoon, and the backstage crew is working long hours too.

38
00:02:58.129 --> 00:03:02.853
If we don't get the sets, lighting, and sound just right, the play will be ruined.

39
00:03:05.015 --> 00:03:08.998
I've learned how to set up the sound system so even people in the rear of the theater

40
00:03:09.038 --> 00:03:10.098
can hear everything.

41
00:03:10.959 --> 00:03:14.142
If there wasn't a sound system, the actors would need to yell!

42
00:03:15.743 --> 00:03:16.824
Lighting is tricky too.

43
00:03:18.816 --> 00:03:22.159
Without it, the audience wouldn't be able to see much onstage.

44
00:03:24.321 --> 00:03:26.662
You have to aim the light where the action is.

45
00:03:29.184 --> 00:03:32.948
It's taken some practice to make sure we move the lights up and down on cue.

46
00:03:34.649 --> 00:03:39.853
And you're not going to believe this: Jae broke his leg playing soccer, so he's out of the

47
00:03:39.913 --> 00:03:42.395
play! Mrs.

48
00:03:42.455 --> 00:03:47.759
Geller asked me to replace him since I've been helping him with his lines and know almost all

49
00:03:47.799 --> 00:03:48.160
of them.

50
00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.802
But I've just gotten the hang of working the sound system.

51
00:03:53.803 --> 00:03:57.466
Working backstage is more fun than I thought, and there's still a lot to do.

52
00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:05.131
We have to design and print programs, put up posters to advertise the play, and take care of

53
00:04:05.331 --> 00:04:06.832
so many more details.

54
00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:10.755
Luckily Mrs.

55
00:04:10.795 --> 00:04:13.837
Geller said Larry could play Romeo if I help him practice.

56
00:04:15.458 --> 00:04:17.339
Whew! Thank you, Larry!

57
00:04:17.939 --> 00:04:23.268
Carlos Hey Marcus!

58
00:04:24.829 --> 00:04:26.070
Too bad you couldn't come!

59
00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.932
The play sold out and the audience loved it.

60
00:04:30.652 --> 00:04:33.473
I think this is our best drama club production ever.

61
00:04:34.594 --> 00:04:38.176
We still have six more performances and they're all sold out.

62
00:04:39.616 --> 00:04:41.818
I hope I get to work backstage again next year.

63
00:04:44.099 --> 00:04:46.460
Well, I have to rush off to the after-play party.

64
00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:53.027
I was talking to Juliet/Rose between scenes, and she said she hoped to see me there.

65
00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:57.273
Just call me backstage Romeo!
